key_responsibilities:
What you will do:
- Deliver outstanding customer support via emails;
- Assisting customers with questions related to shipping, and return policy for damaged items;
- Resolve incomplete orders, change items as needed, and review or approve any price adjustments;
- Responding to customer inquiries in accordance with established service level agreements and follow precise procedures;
- Escalate complex or high-priority issues to the appropriate internal team when needed.

What you need to succeed in this role:
- Excellent English skills (C1 for both spoken and written);
- At least 1 year of experience in a customer support role;
- Experience providing support in an e-commerce environment;
- Hands-on experience with Google Workspace (Docs, Sheets, Drive, Gmail) and basic data entry, website QA, and operational support skills;
- Ability to communicate with customers in a friendly, brand-focused tone, and empathetic manner;
- Strong ability to multitask and switch between tasks seamlessly;
- Be able to provide proper solutions in timely manner, follow SOP's and work independently;
- A customer-focused mindset with a commitment to delivering a positive support experience;
- Commitment to delivering high-quality customer service and meeting performance targets;
- Personal laptop or computer (at least 8Gb of RAM) and a stable internet connection (minimum 50 Mbps-download and 40 Mbps-upload).

Will be a great plus:
- Tech-savvy, with the ability to adapt quickly to new tools and software;
- Experience with Shopify;
- Board game enthusiasm;
- Experience using CRMs or ticketing systems and similar support platforms.

Benefits:
- Schedule: Sunday, and Wednesday to Saturday from 10AM to 6PM (CDT);
- Opportunity to cooperate fully remotely;
- Inclusive international environment;
- Compensation in USD;
- Rewards for referring friends;
- Balance between project workload and personal time, but also -internal health policy;
- Responsive leadership interested in your growth and long-lasting cooperation;
- Greenhouse conditions for self-development;
- A culture built on trust, with no time-tracking requirements.

*The items listed in this section may vary depending on the terms of your engagement. Certain benefits and conditions typically apply to employees; independent contractors may not be eligible for all of these. The specific terms, including compensation, benefits, and work conditions, will be clearly defined in your agreement if selected.

